-- title:
--   Height four from the edge structure constants
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $k$ an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, and let $\iota\colon \mathbb{Z}_{p^2}=W(\mathbb{F}_{p^2})\to W(k)$ be a ring homomorphism (here $\mathbb{Z}_{p^2}$ is `Zp2 p`, the Witt vectors of `GaloisField p 2`). Write $\bar k=W(k)/pW(k)$ for the quotient of $W(k)$ by the ideal generated by $p$, and let $E=$ `EdgeFamily.edgeRingCharP p` $\bar k$ be the edge-chart ring `FormalOmega.chartERing` $\bar k\,(0)\,p$ over $\bar k$. Let $X$ be a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module over $E$: a commutative $2$-dimensional formal group law $F=X.F$ over $E$ together with an action of $\mathbb{Z}_{p^2}$ by endomorphisms of $F$ (unital, multiplicative under composition and additive for the formal addition) and an endomorphism $\varpi$ with $\varpi\circ\varpi=[p]$ and $\varpi\circ a=\sigma(a)\circ\varpi$ for the Frobenius $\sigma$ of $\mathbb{Z}_{p^2}$. Let $\gamma_0,\gamma_1$ be elements of the Cartier module of $F$. Assume (i) $\gamma$ is a homogeneous $V$-basis for the composite $j\colon\mathbb{Z}_{p^2}\xrightarrow{\iota}W(k)\to\bar k\to E$, that is each $\gamma_i$ lies in the graded piece `X.gradedPiece j i` and the matrix of tangent coefficients $(\mathrm{tangent}(\gamma_i)_l)_{i,l}$ has unit determinant; and (ii) $\gamma$ has the edge structure constants $a=$ `EdgeFamily.edgeRingConstants p` $\bar k$, namely for every $i$ and every $N$ there is an element $h$ of the Cartier module with $\varpi_*\gamma_i=\sum_{m<N}V^m\langle a_{m,i}\rangle\gamma_{\mathrm{piIndex}\,m\,i}+V^N h$. Then $X$ has height $4$, i.e. the multiplication-by-$p$ series $X.\mathrm{act}(p)$ has kernel of degree $p^4$ in the sense of `HasKernelOfDegree`.
--
--   This is the height statement for the explicit Čerednik–Drinfeld edge family: the formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module built from the edge structure constants over the reduced edge-chart ring has $p$-torsion of rank $p^4$, as required of a special formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module of height $4$ in Drinfeld's uniformisation. It is used in the assembly of the existence theorem producing, over the edge ring, a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module with a homogeneous $V$-basis, the edge structure constants, speciality and height $4$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_FormalODModule_hasHeight_four_of_hasStructureConstants_edgeRingConstants_of_isAlgClosed.lean

